    "content": "Howard University is a premier private, federally chartered historically Black research university (HBCU) in Washington, D.C., founded in 1867. Ranked #88 in National Universities by U.S. News & World Report, it is an R1 institution known for producing Black STEM PhDs, with a ~41% acceptance rate. Notable alumni include Kamala Harris, Chadwick Boseman, and Thurgood Marshall. Admissions and Academic Information Acceptance Rate: Approximately 41-43%. Admissions Requirements: Test-optional with a 13:1 student-faculty ratio. Ranking: Top-ranked HBCU on U.S. News & World Report’s National Universities list (#88). Academics: Offers over 120 programs; top producer of African-American undergraduates who later earn science and engineering doctoral degrees. Tuition: Approximately $38,936 in tuition and fees, with many students receiving financial aid. Mission and Background Mission: Founded as a comprehensive research-oriented institution, its mission is to provide an educational experience of high quality for students of diverse backgrounds, with a focus on serving the African American community. Location: 257-acre main campus located in northwest Washington, D.C.. Notable Alumni Kamala Harris: 49th Vice President of the United States. Chadwick Boseman: Actor, best known for Black Panther. Thurgood Marshall: First African American Supreme Court Justice. Zora Neale Hurston: Author and anthropologist. Athletics Howard (\"the Bison\") is known for its Division I sports programs, with the men's basketball team recently winning a NCAA tournament game.",
